Exercise 11.3.6: eliminate j
  eliminating j: 1 lower bound(s), 1 upper bound(s) -> at most 1 new rows
    (-i + j - 2 >= 0)  x  (-i - j + 39 >= 0)  =>  -i + 18 >= 0
(a) result  (vars: i j )
    i - 1 >= 0
    -i + 29 >= 0
    -i + 18 >= 0
  eliminating j: 1 lower bound(s), 1 upper bound(s) -> at most 1 new rows
    (-i + j >= 0)  x  (i - j + 9 >= 0)  =>  9 >= 0   [always true, dropped]
(b) result  (vars: i j )
    i - 10 >= 0
    -i + 1000 >= 0
  eliminating j: 1 lower bound(s), 3 upper bound(s) -> at most 3 new rows
    (j >= 0)  x  (i - j + 99 >= 0)  =>  i + 99 >= 0
    (j >= 0)  x  (-i - j + k >= 0)  =>  -i + k >= 0
    (j >= 0)  x  (-i - j - k + 99 >= 0)  =>  -i - k + 99 >= 0
(c) result  (vars: i j k )
    i >= 0
    -i + 99 >= 0
    i + 99 >= 0
    -i + k >= 0
    -i - k + 99 >= 0
